WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:02.105
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.105 --> 00:00:04.040
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.810
between KFC in Japan and the US.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.045
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:10.947 --> 00:00:12.849
So, the fries at the KFC in Japan

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:14.584
come in three sizes.

00:00:14.584 --> 00:00:16.052
So this is small.

00:00:17.187 --> 00:00:19.823
George: Next one is
Joe: And back again!

00:00:19.823 --> 00:00:21.758
George: Large.
Joe: The large.

00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:25.162
Then we got a box.

00:00:29.266 --> 00:00:31.968
Now let's weigh our largest fries.

00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:35.472
Ooh, ooh, ooh!

00:00:35.472 --> 00:00:37.407
[Joe laughs]

00:00:37.407 --> 00:00:38.308
George: We can do it!

00:00:39.976 --> 00:00:40.844
I'm shook!

00:00:40.844 --> 00:00:43.046
As the kids say. By that information.

00:00:43.046 --> 00:00:45.582
I want to say, though,
that theirs is a box.

00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:47.784
That thing is, like, made to be eaten

00:00:47.784 --> 00:00:49.319
by more than one person, I'm assuming.

00:00:49.319 --> 00:00:50.420
But this, clearly,

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.955
this is for a person. So.

00:00:51.955 --> 00:00:54.458
So, in Japan, we have three drink sizes.

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:56.092
So we have a small.

00:00:56.092 --> 00:00:57.327
In the US, our drinks come

00:00:57.327 --> 00:00:59.463
in medium.
George: A medium.

00:00:59.463 --> 00:01:01.465
Then we got a large.

00:01:01.465 --> 00:01:02.833
And large.

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:06.770
So, in Japan, KFC doesn't disclose

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:09.639
how much liquid is in each of the sizes.

00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:10.607
Why?

00:01:10.607 --> 00:01:12.943
So I will help you, KFC.

00:01:12.943 --> 00:01:15.278
We will measure the cups right now.

00:01:15.278 --> 00:01:16.346
Let's go.

00:01:23.086 --> 00:01:25.121
So now let's measure our large,

00:01:25.121 --> 00:01:26.356
and just to make sure it's accurate,

00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:27.991
we didn't clean the measuring cup.

00:01:34.097 --> 00:01:34.931
Go home.

00:01:38.668 --> 00:01:40.136
So, at the KFC in Japan,

00:01:40.136 --> 00:01:42.873
you can order your chicken pieces in

00:01:42.873 --> 00:01:43.740
one piece,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.641
two pieces,

00:01:44.641 --> 00:01:46.776
three pieces,

00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:48.445
four pieces,

00:01:48.445 --> 00:01:50.380
and six pieces,

00:01:52.115 --> 00:01:54.317
and eight pieces,

00:01:56.653 --> 00:01:58.922
and 10 pieces,

00:01:59.856 --> 00:02:02.759
and 12 pieces.

00:02:04.594 --> 00:02:05.695
KFC in the US,

00:02:05.695 --> 00:02:07.197
our chicken portion sizes

00:02:07.197 --> 00:02:09.332
start as a two-piece combo.

00:02:09.332 --> 00:02:11.201
By the way, come on, guys.

00:02:11.201 --> 00:02:13.103
This isn't whatever
this is supposed to be.

00:02:13.103 --> 00:02:15.238
Then the three-piece
right in front of me here.

00:02:15.238 --> 00:02:16.406
And that's the exact opposite.

00:02:16.406 --> 00:02:17.841
I went extra crispy for this.

00:02:17.841 --> 00:02:19.910
Look at the size of these chicken pieces!

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.845
Yes, yes to these.

00:02:21.845 --> 00:02:23.413
And the four-piece.

00:02:23.413 --> 00:02:24.648
This is somewhere in the middle.

00:02:24.648 --> 00:02:26.149
Each combo comes with a biscuit,

00:02:26.149 --> 00:02:27.217
your choice of potato,

00:02:27.217 --> 00:02:29.886
either fries or mashed with gravy,

00:02:29.886 --> 00:02:31.988
and all of them come with a medium drink.

00:02:31.988 --> 00:02:33.189
But we don't stop there.

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:34.524
We go now to buckets,

00:02:34.524 --> 00:02:36.560
where you can get an eight-piece bucket,

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.928
12-piece bucket,

00:02:37.928 --> 00:02:39.529
or a 16-piece bucket.

00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:43.366
So, now we are going to weigh

00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:45.001
our eight-piece chicken

00:02:45.001 --> 00:02:47.671
to compare the weights in each country.

00:02:47.671 --> 00:02:50.407
Joe: Ooh, ooh, oh!

00:02:50.407 --> 00:02:54.177
Oh, this is the — ugh!

00:02:54.177 --> 00:02:55.779
Yo!

00:02:55.779 --> 00:02:56.780
It's pretty close!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.082
Considering all the variables of

00:02:59.082 --> 00:03:00.784
size of chicken,

00:03:00.784 --> 00:03:03.286
bone density, batter.

00:03:03.286 --> 00:03:04.654
I don't know what I'm talking about,

00:03:04.654 --> 00:03:06.356
but that's surprisingly close.

00:03:06.356 --> 00:03:09.159
So, in Japan, a two-piece
of original chicken,

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:11.027
which are breasts and wing

00:03:11.027 --> 00:03:13.630
and small fries and a medium drink,

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:17.867
costs 800 yen, or $7.27.

00:03:17.867 --> 00:03:18.702
So, in Japan,

00:03:18.702 --> 00:03:22.205
actually KFC is considered
a little bit more expensive

00:03:22.205 --> 00:03:25.108
compared to other fast-food
chains, like McDonald's.

00:03:25.108 --> 00:03:28.378
So it's a classic fast food in Japan.

00:03:28.378 --> 00:03:31.881
That same meal is about $8.99,

00:03:31.881 --> 00:03:35.752
or in Japanese yen, 992.27.

00:03:35.752 --> 00:03:39.322
So that's about a 24%
cost increase in the US.

00:03:39.322 --> 00:03:42.058
So, in Japan, to make chicken at KFC,

00:03:42.058 --> 00:03:45.528
you must be certified
as a chicken specialist,

00:03:45.528 --> 00:03:47.931
and certification takes three months,

00:03:47.931 --> 00:03:51.568
and your knowledge and
skills are tested every year.

00:03:51.568 --> 00:03:53.003
All right, so let's take

00:03:53.003 --> 00:03:55.505
the chicken-specialist test right now.

00:03:55.505 --> 00:03:56.706
All right, George, let's do this.

00:03:56.706 --> 00:03:57.641
No. 1.

00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:00.777
"For the original chicken,
100% domestic ... "

00:04:00.777 --> 00:04:02.679
That's kind of a bummer.

00:04:02.679 --> 00:04:03.747
Hmm.

00:04:03.747 --> 00:04:05.415
I'm just gonna — yeah. Ba ba de ba ba ba.

00:04:05.415 --> 00:04:06.549
Animal fat or vegetable oil ...

00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:08.551
Fried with a lighter weight.

00:04:08.551 --> 00:04:11.821
With a lighter weight than —
these got hard fast.

00:04:11.821 --> 00:04:14.457
Beep, beep, beep, beep, beep ...

00:04:14.457 --> 00:04:15.692
I am in over my head on this one.

00:04:15.692 --> 00:04:17.260
I don't even know what that means.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.361
All right, so just now

00:04:18.361 --> 00:04:20.563
I've got all of the five answers,

00:04:20.563 --> 00:04:22.966
so let's check answers.

00:04:22.966 --> 00:04:25.468
Gold chicken certification.

00:04:25.468 --> 00:04:26.770
Gold!

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.772
[applause]

00:04:28.772 --> 00:04:29.606
Oof!

00:04:29.606 --> 00:04:31.241
Says "Not KFC material,"

00:04:31.241 --> 00:04:34.177
and it's a picture of Colonel
Sanders giving me the finger.

00:04:34.177 --> 00:04:36.146
So I'm gonna assume I did not pass it.

00:04:36.146 --> 00:04:38.915
But anyway, I've got gold.

00:04:38.915 --> 00:04:40.850
I'm the champion!

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:41.951
I am very surprised by that.

00:04:41.951 --> 00:04:43.653
I think I could work for KFC.

00:04:43.653 --> 00:04:46.823
I mean, I kind of look like
Colonel Sanders, right?

00:04:46.823 --> 00:04:48.525
Look at this guy.

00:04:48.525 --> 00:04:50.260
I'm a younger Colonel Sanders.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.795
KFC is doing any sort of

00:04:51.795 --> 00:04:55.365
"The Adventures of Young
Colonel Sanders" ad campaign.

00:04:55.365 --> 00:04:57.167
Is this a face that can sell chicken?

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.102
Yeah! Haven't you guys
ever read the secret?

00:04:59.102 --> 00:05:00.336
I'm putting the energy that I want

00:05:00.336 --> 00:05:02.272
out into the universe,
and it comes back to me.

00:05:02.272 --> 00:05:03.573
Conner: Manifesting.

00:05:03.573 --> 00:05:05.308
It's called manifesting.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.179
So, here is everything you can only find

00:05:09.179 --> 00:05:11.414
on the menu at the KFC in Japan,

00:05:11.414 --> 00:05:12.949
but not in the US.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:15.285
And here is everything
you can find on the menu

00:05:15.285 --> 00:05:17.754
at a US KFC you cannot get in Japan.

00:05:17.754 --> 00:05:21.324
Here, we've got KFC biscuits.

00:05:21.324 --> 00:05:22.325
Both places have biscuits,

00:05:22.325 --> 00:05:23.727
but their biscuit has a hole in it.

00:05:23.727 --> 00:05:25.328
And it looks a lot fluffier. Right?

00:05:25.328 --> 00:05:26.496
Our biscuit, on the other hand,

00:05:26.496 --> 00:05:28.465
is just this Southern style.

00:05:28.465 --> 00:05:29.699
Not exactly a scone,

00:05:29.699 --> 00:05:31.301
but kind of looks like
one from a distance.

00:05:31.301 --> 00:05:33.336
Dry cornmeal biscuit.

00:05:33.336 --> 00:05:36.806
It comes with honey maple KFC.

00:05:36.806 --> 00:05:40.243
George: Ahh.
Joe: Oh, ho ho ho ho!

00:05:40.243 --> 00:05:41.344
Yeah.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:44.948
This is good.

00:05:44.948 --> 00:05:47.717
The maple is a little bit sweet for me.

00:05:47.717 --> 00:05:48.718
Mac and cheese.

00:05:48.718 --> 00:05:50.820
I can't believe you guys do
not have macaroni and cheese.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.655
Mwah. Love mac and cheese.

00:05:52.655 --> 00:05:54.190
Mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.325
You don't have that in Japan?

00:05:55.325 --> 00:05:56.159
Guys.

00:05:56.159 --> 00:05:56.993
Guys!

00:05:56.993 --> 00:05:59.929
Demand this from your Japanese KFC.

00:05:59.929 --> 00:06:01.431
You want the mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:06:01.431 --> 00:06:04.534
So, we also have dip packs.

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:06.369
Ooh.

00:06:06.369 --> 00:06:08.905
So, it's got Colonel Crispy,

00:06:08.905 --> 00:06:10.974
and some nuggets,

00:06:10.974 --> 00:06:13.443
and boneless Kentucky,

00:06:13.443 --> 00:06:15.879
and some original chicken.

00:06:15.879 --> 00:06:17.447
So this dip pack,

00:06:17.447 --> 00:06:18.982
it comes with this fries

00:06:18.982 --> 00:06:20.316
and also

00:06:20.316 --> 00:06:23.720
these three dipping sauces.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.322
And now for the quickest Sauce Talk ever.

00:06:26.322 --> 00:06:27.223
Sauce Talk.

00:06:27.223 --> 00:06:28.124
KFC sauce.

00:06:31.461 --> 00:06:34.197
I think the KFC sauce is
like a brown mustard mayo.

00:06:34.197 --> 00:06:35.799
Yeah, that sauce is good.

00:06:35.799 --> 00:06:37.967
So, we've got

00:06:37.967 --> 00:06:38.935
barbecue sauce

00:06:38.935 --> 00:06:41.070
and mustard,

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:44.474
and this pink one is called mentaiko mayo.

00:06:44.474 --> 00:06:47.443
Mentaiko means it's spicy cod roe,

00:06:47.443 --> 00:06:50.180
and it's very popular at KFC in Japan.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.281
This is actually great.

00:06:51.281 --> 00:06:52.949
I'll dip this.

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:53.783
Mm!

00:06:56.553 --> 00:06:59.122
It tastes fantastic.

00:06:59.122 --> 00:07:00.990
Winner!

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:03.726
So, if you want to have
a little bigger one,

00:07:03.726 --> 00:07:05.862
you can order dip barrel.

00:07:05.862 --> 00:07:08.464
I mean, it's double
amount of this dip pack,

00:07:08.464 --> 00:07:09.866
so it's going to be very big.

00:07:09.866 --> 00:07:12.368
So, this one right here is called

00:07:12.368 --> 00:07:14.504
four-piece red hot chicken box,

00:07:14.504 --> 00:07:18.041
and it comes with a pie and fry,

00:07:18.041 --> 00:07:20.743
and a medium drink.

00:07:20.743 --> 00:07:23.913
And actually we have other box options,

00:07:23.913 --> 00:07:27.617
like four-piece half hot
and half original box.

00:07:27.617 --> 00:07:29.953
And it comes with fries as well.

00:07:29.953 --> 00:07:34.290
And six-piece half hot
and half original box.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.859
It comes with fries again.

00:07:37.794 --> 00:07:40.430
So, in Japan, we have tori no hi pack.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.198
That means chicken day.

00:07:42.198 --> 00:07:45.401
It's on every 28th of the month.

00:07:45.401 --> 00:07:48.071
And two stands for ni,

00:07:48.071 --> 00:07:51.040
and eight stands for wa.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:52.842
And it becomes niwa,

00:07:52.842 --> 00:07:56.212
and niwa is synonmous with niwatori.

00:07:56.212 --> 00:07:58.481
Niwatori means chicken.

00:07:58.481 --> 00:08:01.184
So that's why it's called chicken day.

00:08:01.184 --> 00:08:06.155
KFC in America has extra-crispy chicken.

00:08:06.155 --> 00:08:07.457
This is the best type of chicken.

00:08:07.457 --> 00:08:08.324
I mean, look at this.

00:08:08.324 --> 00:08:09.592
I don't know what they do to this,

00:08:09.592 --> 00:08:11.828
but the skin is practically falling off.

00:08:11.828 --> 00:08:14.197
It is so crispy and so delicious.

00:08:14.197 --> 00:08:16.032
I love extra crispy so much.

00:08:16.032 --> 00:08:17.667
I got this little guy.

00:08:17.667 --> 00:08:19.068
The Chicken Little. Look at this guy.

00:08:19.068 --> 00:08:20.470
Eh? Look at this little guy.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.372
Comes with pickles, mayo.

00:08:22.372 --> 00:08:24.007
The pot pie that they have here,

00:08:24.007 --> 00:08:26.976
they're not kidding when they
say "pie" in the pot pie.

00:08:26.976 --> 00:08:27.944
Look how thick this is!

00:08:27.944 --> 00:08:29.812
Speaking of big dishes of stuff,

00:08:29.812 --> 00:08:31.347
the Famous Bowl.

00:08:31.347 --> 00:08:34.684
Once upon a time, a KFC employee was like,

00:08:34.684 --> 00:08:37.954
I'm gonna put everything into
one dish and call it a day.

00:08:37.954 --> 00:08:40.089
And ta-da, the Famous Bowl was born.

00:08:40.089 --> 00:08:42.325
This has to be, like, 3 pounds.

00:08:42.325 --> 00:08:44.460
All right, so here we've got

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.663
two special twisters.

00:08:46.663 --> 00:08:49.132
So this one right here is called

00:08:49.132 --> 00:08:51.067
pepper mayonnaise twister.

00:08:51.067 --> 00:08:53.703
Ooh! It looks great.

00:08:56.873 --> 00:08:59.075
[applause]

00:08:59.075 --> 00:09:00.777
9 out of 10.

00:09:00.777 --> 00:09:02.745
KFC, thank you!

00:09:02.745 --> 00:09:04.747
Thank you for making me happy.

00:09:04.747 --> 00:09:06.282
So, next, we've got,

00:09:06.282 --> 00:09:07.150
ooh!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.152
Teriyaki twister.

00:09:09.152 --> 00:09:10.620
Should be great.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:11.888
It's kind of gross.

00:09:11.888 --> 00:09:13.122
[laughs]

00:09:13.122 --> 00:09:15.992
It's got mayo and Colonel Crispy,

00:09:15.992 --> 00:09:17.193
some veggies,

00:09:17.193 --> 00:09:20.530
and I hope this is teriyaki sauce.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.631
Itadakimasu!

00:09:25.134 --> 00:09:28.905
Mm. Mm! Mm!

00:09:28.905 --> 00:09:33.643
It looks gross, but it tastes incredible.

00:09:33.643 --> 00:09:37.380
10 out of 10. Congratulations.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.815
Oishii!

00:09:38.815 --> 00:09:40.216
It means delicious!

00:09:40.216 --> 00:09:41.951
Look how tiny those twisters are.

00:09:41.951 --> 00:09:44.520
I could eat, like, three
of those easily. Easily!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.856
All right, so we have nuggets.

00:09:46.856 --> 00:09:49.425
We have three pieces,

00:09:49.425 --> 00:09:51.060
five pieces,

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:54.397
and they come with only ketchup.

00:09:54.397 --> 00:09:56.632
Also at a US KFC that
you can't get in Japan

00:09:56.632 --> 00:09:57.600
are wings.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.202
You can get wings at the KFC

00:09:59.202 --> 00:10:03.439
in units of six, 12, 24 or 48.

00:10:03.439 --> 00:10:06.476
I believe the three wing
flavors that I got here are

00:10:06.476 --> 00:10:07.877
standard Buffalo,

00:10:07.877 --> 00:10:10.013
the honey barbecue,

00:10:10.013 --> 00:10:11.914
and if you're a total wuss,

00:10:11.914 --> 00:10:13.149
unsauced?

00:10:13.149 --> 00:10:14.484
What's wrong with you?

00:10:14.484 --> 00:10:15.785
Yeah. Very sketchy.

00:10:15.785 --> 00:10:18.921
You can also get them, in a limited time,

00:10:18.921 --> 00:10:20.456
Nashville hot sauce.

00:10:20.456 --> 00:10:24.127
Now we have special sandwiches.

00:10:24.127 --> 00:10:25.628
This one right here is called

00:10:25.628 --> 00:10:28.331
Japanese-style chicken katsu sandwich.

00:10:28.331 --> 00:10:30.199
So let's take a look inside.

00:10:30.199 --> 00:10:31.300
So, it's got mayo,

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:33.002
and it's got cabbage,

00:10:33.002 --> 00:10:35.304
and chicken katsu right there.

00:10:35.304 --> 00:10:36.406
Itadakimasu!

00:10:38.508 --> 00:10:39.976
Mm.

00:10:39.976 --> 00:10:40.810
Oh!

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.713
This sauce is soy-sauce-based sauce,

00:10:43.713 --> 00:10:44.981
and it's a little bit sweet.

00:10:44.981 --> 00:10:47.917
And this mayo is also
great with this sauce.

00:10:47.917 --> 00:10:49.819
This looks really small,

00:10:49.819 --> 00:10:52.789
but it has huge amount of chicken.

00:10:52.789 --> 00:10:55.324
So if you eat this, you're gonna be full.

00:10:56.225 --> 00:11:00.063
And next one, we've got chicken fillet.

00:11:00.063 --> 00:11:02.665
Wow. This is also huge.

00:11:02.665 --> 00:11:04.734
All right, so this one right here

00:11:04.734 --> 00:11:07.870
is called black hot sandwich.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.605
Ooh!

00:11:09.605 --> 00:11:12.108
Look at this. It's, like, pepper mayo?

00:11:12.108 --> 00:11:14.343
I just tasted this pepper mayo,

00:11:14.343 --> 00:11:17.313
but it has a little, like, spiciness.

00:11:17.313 --> 00:11:19.215
Ooh, ho ho.

00:11:19.215 --> 00:11:21.851
Oh, man. It's too strong.

00:11:21.851 --> 00:11:24.087
I wouldn't get it. Be careful.

00:11:24.087 --> 00:11:27.623
Now, of course, the US
has a chicken sandwich.

00:11:27.623 --> 00:11:29.459
But our chicken sandwich
and their chicken sandwich,

00:11:29.459 --> 00:11:30.960
as you can see, is way different.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.629
You can also get it spicy or classic.

00:11:33.629 --> 00:11:34.464
This is a classic.

00:11:34.464 --> 00:11:35.998
All right, so this one right here

00:11:35.998 --> 00:11:38.367
is called Colonel Crispy.

00:11:38.367 --> 00:11:39.669
Is it only in Japan?

00:11:39.669 --> 00:11:41.671
I cannot confirm the difference between

00:11:41.671 --> 00:11:44.407
a Colonel Crispy and a KFC chicken tender.

00:11:44.407 --> 00:11:46.676
They call their tenders Colonel Crispies,

00:11:46.676 --> 00:11:50.113
and we call our Colonel
Crispies chicken tenders.

00:11:50.113 --> 00:11:52.748
It's been a while since
I ordered this one,

00:11:52.748 --> 00:11:55.585
but it still has crispy bits.

00:11:56.986 --> 00:11:57.820
Good job.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:02.391
Japanese KFC's technology,
state of the art.

00:12:02.391 --> 00:12:05.394
We currently have a Nashville hot chicken

00:12:05.394 --> 00:12:06.395
and hot tenders.

00:12:06.395 --> 00:12:07.597
I went ahead with the tenders.

00:12:07.597 --> 00:12:08.431
I've just been informed

00:12:08.431 --> 00:12:09.932
this was a big TikTok thing for a minute.

00:12:09.932 --> 00:12:11.367
Something about biting
it and crunching it.

00:12:11.367 --> 00:12:12.468
I don't know anything about that.

00:12:12.468 --> 00:12:13.803
I can say just by holding this,

00:12:13.803 --> 00:12:15.538
there's no way these are crispy.

00:12:15.538 --> 00:12:16.372
[crunching]

00:12:17.707 --> 00:12:18.941
Was not that spicy.

00:12:18.941 --> 00:12:19.876
That's kind of spicy.

00:12:19.876 --> 00:12:21.244
I do like this a lot.

00:12:24.313 --> 00:12:25.915
I can't stop eating it.

00:12:25.915 --> 00:12:28.484
Ooh. That heat's catching up with me.

00:12:28.484 --> 00:12:30.019
Slow burn. Slow build on the heat.

00:12:30.019 --> 00:12:33.189
So, here we've got
Japanese exclusive drinks.

00:12:33.189 --> 00:12:36.025
This one right here is

00:12:36.025 --> 00:12:36.993
water,

00:12:37.994 --> 00:12:42.365
but it comes with this Assam tea pack.

00:12:43.232 --> 00:12:46.269
It's supposed to be hot, but it's cold.

00:12:46.269 --> 00:12:48.871
And next one, we've got coffee.

00:12:48.871 --> 00:12:51.040
So, this one right here is

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:53.075
roasted rich coffee.

00:12:53.075 --> 00:12:54.076
Itadakimasu.

00:12:56.546 --> 00:13:00.082
It's a little bit better
than the normal coffee.

00:13:00.082 --> 00:13:04.020
And here we've got Earl Grey iced tea.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.221
It's not sweet at all.

00:13:05.221 --> 00:13:08.157
And next one is melon soda.

00:13:08.157 --> 00:13:10.426
It has bright green color.

00:13:15.064 --> 00:13:16.966
Horrible. It's too sweet.

00:13:16.966 --> 00:13:19.368
Here is ginger ale.

00:13:19.368 --> 00:13:20.403
Nothing special.

00:13:20.403 --> 00:13:21.871
And the last one,

00:13:21.871 --> 00:13:24.373
it's Nacchan refreshing orange.

00:13:24.373 --> 00:13:26.309
Fountain drinks. There's
a few that we can get

00:13:26.309 --> 00:13:28.811
that you guys cannot over there in Japan.

00:13:28.811 --> 00:13:31.581
The first one is a beverage that

00:13:31.581 --> 00:13:35.484
I have yet to meet one
human being who enjoys it.

00:13:35.484 --> 00:13:37.153
Of course, I'm talking about Sierra Mist.

00:13:37.153 --> 00:13:38.921
Maybe grossest soda ever.

00:13:40.823 --> 00:13:42.458
Oh, it's so bad.

00:13:42.458 --> 00:13:44.727
Another drink that you can get at KFC

00:13:44.727 --> 00:13:45.962
that you can't get at Japan,

00:13:45.962 --> 00:13:46.963
and here it is right here,

00:13:46.963 --> 00:13:48.231
Mountain Dew's great.

00:13:48.231 --> 00:13:49.999
When I was in college, I
worked at a pizza place.

00:13:49.999 --> 00:13:51.867
I drank so much Mountain Dew, I threw up.

00:13:51.867 --> 00:13:52.868
And now I'm drinking Mountain Dew.

00:13:52.868 --> 00:13:53.970
Let's see if I can do it again.

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.440
My favorite beverage,
Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

00:13:58.941 --> 00:14:00.209
So good. So good.

00:14:00.209 --> 00:14:03.546
So, drinks are just
normal, nothing special,

00:14:03.546 --> 00:14:05.881
but chickens are

00:14:05.881 --> 00:14:07.717
finger-licking good.

00:14:08.784 --> 00:14:10.086
Desserts at a US KFC,

00:14:10.086 --> 00:14:12.054
you can get this chocolate chip cookie.

00:14:12.054 --> 00:14:13.956
Recognize that guy?

00:14:13.956 --> 00:14:15.791
I just look just like this guy.

00:14:15.791 --> 00:14:17.727
And, finally,

00:14:17.727 --> 00:14:19.262
a chocolate chip cake.

00:14:21.397 --> 00:14:23.799
So, let's talk about Christmas in Japan.

00:14:23.799 --> 00:14:27.536
So Christmas is one of the
biggest events in Japan,

00:14:27.536 --> 00:14:31.807
even though about 1% of
Japanese people are Christians.

00:14:31.807 --> 00:14:35.611
We just enter Christmas
as just a fun event.

00:14:35.611 --> 00:14:38.481
And as for KFC for Christmas in Japan,

00:14:38.481 --> 00:14:40.950
back in 1970s,

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:42.852
Japan KFC launched

00:14:42.852 --> 00:14:46.622
a hugely successful advertising campaign

00:14:46.622 --> 00:14:48.591
called Kentakki ni wa Kurisumasu.

00:14:48.591 --> 00:14:51.093
That's Kentucky for Christmas.

00:14:51.093 --> 00:14:54.196
And with that strong marketing campaign,

00:14:54.196 --> 00:14:55.631
it became so popular

00:14:55.631 --> 00:14:58.501
to have KFC for Christmas in Japan.

00:14:58.501 --> 00:15:02.571
And now about 3.6
million Japanese families

00:15:02.571 --> 00:15:04.273
eat KFC for Christmas.

00:15:04.273 --> 00:15:06.742
And talking about my personal experiences,

00:15:06.742 --> 00:15:08.277
yes, when I was young,

00:15:08.277 --> 00:15:11.614
I would eat KFC for
Christmas with my family.

00:15:11.614 --> 00:15:14.116
But when you started dating, you know,

00:15:14.116 --> 00:15:16.319
Christmas makes the transformation

00:15:16.319 --> 00:15:20.189
from a family event to couple's event.

00:15:20.189 --> 00:15:22.124
And I'm looking for the one

00:15:22.124 --> 00:15:25.227
who can enjoy KFC for Christmas with me.

00:15:27.163 --> 00:15:29.999
So, in Japan, one drumstick of ori —

00:15:29.999 --> 00:15:31.400
ooh!

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:35.104
So, in Japan, one drumstick
of original chicken,

00:15:35.104 --> 00:15:38.741
on average, has 237 calories.

00:15:38.741 --> 00:15:41.277
Chicken's looking a
little limp there, George.

00:15:41.277 --> 00:15:45.481
In the US, one stiff
drumstick of original recipe

00:15:45.481 --> 00:15:46.949
is 130 calories.

00:15:46.949 --> 00:15:49.352
But according to KFC's US site,

00:15:49.352 --> 00:15:51.354
that's for a 53-gram piece.

00:15:51.354 --> 00:15:53.956
Now, adjusting for the 87-gram piece,

00:15:53.956 --> 00:15:55.024
like that of Japan,

00:15:55.024 --> 00:15:57.693
the calories go up to 210.

00:15:57.693 --> 00:15:59.095
Does that make sense? Great.

00:15:59.095 --> 00:16:01.597
Now, take this bad boy
and make him extra crispy?

00:16:01.597 --> 00:16:04.133
You got 270 calories.

00:16:04.133 --> 00:16:07.603
So, in Japan, a two-piece
of original chickens

00:16:07.603 --> 00:16:09.805
and a small fry and a medium drink

00:16:09.805 --> 00:16:13.576
is roughly 717 calories.

00:16:13.576 --> 00:16:16.612
A US two-piece, individual
fry, and medium drink

00:16:16.612 --> 00:16:19.482
comes out to be 990 calories.

00:16:19.482 --> 00:16:20.816
So a lot more.

00:16:20.816 --> 00:16:22.952
It's too many calories.

00:16:22.952 --> 00:16:24.720
Mm.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.188
Not enough calories, if you ask me.

00:16:26.188 --> 00:16:28.457
But finger-licking good.

00:16:28.457 --> 00:16:29.959
I think KFC got to George.

00:16:29.959 --> 00:16:31.427
He keeps dropping that slogan.

00:16:31.427 --> 00:16:32.294
Are they paying George?

00:16:32.294 --> 00:16:34.864
I think George is getting some
money on the side from KFC.

00:16:34.864 --> 00:16:35.698
Oh, my God.

00:16:35.698 --> 00:16:37.233
If George turns out to be Colonel Sanders,

00:16:37.233 --> 00:16:38.601
I will lose my mind.

00:16:40.169 --> 00:16:43.572
So, KFC in Japan doesn't
disclose their ingredients.

00:16:43.572 --> 00:16:46.275
So we emailed their customer support,

00:16:46.275 --> 00:16:48.344
and this is what they told us.

00:16:50.546 --> 00:16:51.380
And in the US,

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:53.416
our original-recipe
chicken ingredients are:

00:16:53.416 --> 00:16:54.750
first, with the fresh chicken,

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:57.686
it is marinated with
salt, sodium phosphate,

00:16:57.686 --> 00:16:59.221
and monosodium glutamate.

00:16:59.221 --> 00:17:00.055
On to the breading,

00:17:00.055 --> 00:17:01.791
it's breaded with wheat flour,

00:17:01.791 --> 00:17:03.058
tricalcium phosphate,

00:17:03.058 --> 00:17:04.126
maltodextrin,

00:17:04.126 --> 00:17:05.027
triglycerides,

00:17:05.027 --> 00:17:06.162
natural flavor,

00:17:06.162 --> 00:17:09.865
Colonel's secret original
recipe seasoning.

00:17:09.865 --> 00:17:14.136
They also said our fries are
made of potatoes, obviously,

00:17:14.136 --> 00:17:15.805
and vegetable oil and fat.

00:17:15.805 --> 00:17:18.307
The batter is made of rice flour,

00:17:18.307 --> 00:17:19.408
vegetable starch,

00:17:19.408 --> 00:17:21.076
and dextrose.

00:17:21.076 --> 00:17:21.911
And our fries,

00:17:21.911 --> 00:17:23.245
which contain sea salt,

00:17:23.245 --> 00:17:24.513
monosodium glutamate,

00:17:24.513 --> 00:17:25.781
tricalcium phosphate,

00:17:25.781 --> 00:17:27.283
hydrolyzed soy protein,

00:17:27.283 --> 00:17:28.717
potassium chloride,

00:17:28.717 --> 00:17:30.152
potatoes, that's good,

00:17:30.152 --> 00:17:31.687
degermed yellow cornmeal,

00:17:31.687 --> 00:17:35.124
disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate,

00:17:35.124 --> 00:17:37.026
to maintain natural color.

00:17:37.026 --> 00:17:37.993
What's more natural

00:17:37.993 --> 00:17:40.296
than disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate?

00:17:40.296 --> 00:17:41.564
Rolls off the tongue.

00:17:41.564 --> 00:17:43.098
And one thing I have to say

00:17:43.098 --> 00:17:45.568
is that our fries are imported

00:17:45.568 --> 00:17:47.837
from both America and Belgium.

00:17:47.837 --> 00:17:50.539
And some of the Belgian fries

00:17:50.539 --> 00:17:53.342
are made with potatoes from France.

00:17:53.342 --> 00:17:57.980
So our fries are truly, truly French.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:17:59.114
Bonjour!

00:17:59.114 --> 00:18:03.319
In the US, we have four chicken shapes.

00:18:03.319 --> 00:18:06.222
In Japan, we have five chicken shapes.

00:18:06.222 --> 00:18:07.223
Let me explain.

00:18:07.223 --> 00:18:09.425
So, we have this one.

00:18:09.425 --> 00:18:10.826
It's called kiru.

00:18:10.826 --> 00:18:15.698
Kiru is like chicken's breast, right here.

00:18:17.366 --> 00:18:18.367
[laughing]

00:18:18.367 --> 00:18:21.470
I'm gonna say chicken's chest.

00:18:21.470 --> 00:18:22.571
Breasts ...

00:18:22.571 --> 00:18:24.139
[laughing]

00:18:27.243 --> 00:18:31.347
Kiru is like chicken's chest, right there.

00:18:31.347 --> 00:18:32.615
The first one is the breast.

00:18:32.615 --> 00:18:34.283
This is the big piece of
chicken your dad gets.

00:18:34.283 --> 00:18:36.752
And also we got wing.

00:18:36.752 --> 00:18:39.822
It's a, as you know, chicken wing.

00:18:39.822 --> 00:18:41.490
This is supposed to be a wing.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:43.726
This is laughably small.

00:18:43.726 --> 00:18:45.661
And we've got this one.

00:18:45.661 --> 00:18:46.962
It's called rib.

00:18:46.962 --> 00:18:47.897
Chickens have ribs?

00:18:47.897 --> 00:18:52.201
So, rib is, like, under
the chest, right here.

00:18:52.201 --> 00:18:54.203
And we got this one, thigh.

00:18:54.203 --> 00:18:56.305
Thigh is, like, chicken's lower back.

00:18:57.239 --> 00:19:00.976
And the next piece is this,
which I think is the thigh.

00:19:00.976 --> 00:19:02.778
And, of course,

00:19:02.778 --> 00:19:04.647
the next piece, everyone knows the drum.

00:19:04.647 --> 00:19:06.882
And this is a chicken's leg.

00:19:06.882 --> 00:19:08.717
Hey, if you enjoyed watching this episode

00:19:08.717 --> 00:19:10.819
of US versus Japan KFC,

00:19:10.819 --> 00:19:11.887
we actually have another series

00:19:11.887 --> 00:19:13.355
comparing the US and the UK,

00:19:13.355 --> 00:19:16.292
and you can watch that
KFC episode right here.

